# What's on Sunshine coast

## _African Children's Choir - Under One Sky Concert June 20th 2015_

Now this is going to be an absolutely brilliant show right here on the Sunshine Coast and has been touring for over 30 years! Do not miss this and be in the chance to win a free double pass! All you have to do is turn up to our event 2pm May 30th , The Last Saturplay @ Renae's Pantry, The Lane, Palmwoods and you will go in the draw! See [here](/eats-drinks-drums-and-good-vibes/?utm_source=Contacts+May+2015&utm_campaign=552d2b05b4-Rhythm_Culture_Newsletter_Oct_201410_6_2014&utm_medium=email&utm_term=0_e16109c64d-552d2b05b4-119840849) for more event info! _[Lake Kawana Community Centre](http://www.scvenuesandevents.com.au/lake-kawana-community-centre)_ _Sat 20 June 2015_

_**Time:**_

_Doors 6pm / Show 7pm to 9pm_

_**Tickets:**_

_Adults $30 / Concession $25 / Student $25 / Children (5-12yrs) $20 / Under 5 years free / Adult Group 10 $270 / Concession Group 10 $225 / Family of 3 $60 / Family of 4 (min 2 children) $90 / Family of 5 (min 2 adults) $105_

_Sunshine Coast residents will be treated to a unique musical experience when the African Children’s Choir returns with its vibrant and outstanding musical and dancing performance at Lake Kawana Community Centre in June._ _The concert will be an exclusive double bill, featuring highly acclaimed dynamic looping artist **Mr Percival** as support act, with guest appearance by **Cool Harmonies Community Choir**._ _The African Children’s Choir is comprised of orphaned and vulnerable children from the disadvantaged Kampala and Luwero areas of Uganda._ _Their vibrancy, outstanding musical and dancing abilities have captured the world’s imagination since the choir started touring North America and Europe 30 years ago to raise money for children’s education._ _The African Children’s Choir is returning to Australia following its inaugural visit in 2013, with sell out concerts and workshops across eastern Australia, including the Sunshine Coast._ _Cool Harmonies community choir will again host the 18 children and eight chaperones from the Uganda-based choir who will present a fun filled evening of singing, drumming and dancing as they spread their message of hope and joy for their future._ _The Sunshine Coast visit is part of a three-month tour across three States, visiting Geelong, Melbourne, Albury, Canberra, Wollongong, Sydney, Nowra, Laurieton, Port Macquarie, Taree, Bellingen, Mullumbimby, Gold Coast, and Brisbane._ _Meet the kids preparing for their tour to Australia: [http://vimeo.com/98395905](http://vimeo.com/98395905)_ _**Under One Sky Concert**_ _Where: Lake Kawana Community Centre_ _When: Saturday, 20 June 2015_ _Time: 7pm - 9pm_   _**Tickets**_ _$30 Adult_  _$25 Concession_  _$25 Students_ _$20 Children (5-12yrs)_  _$270 Adult Group 10_  _$225 Concession Group 10_  _$60 Family of 3 (1 Adult & 2 children or 2 adults and 1 child)_  _$90 Family of 4 (min 2 children)_  _$105 Family of 5 (min 2 adults)_
